cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Prot2Vec: a benchmark harness for protein sequence embeddings"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kunapareddy
    given-names: Sai Nikhil
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikhil-kunapareddy/Prot2Vec"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
abstract: >-
  Prot2Vec benchmarks protein sequence embedding methods on protein family
  separability. It compares amino acid composition, k-mer TF-IDF, ESM-2 protein
  language models and general-purpose LLM embedding APIs across PCA, UMAP and
  t-SNE projections, scoring every pair with family-separability,
  homology-retrieval, clustering-agreement and projection-trustworthiness
  metrics against curated Pfam seed alignments or user-supplied FASTA.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - proteomics
  - protein embeddings
  - protein language models
  - representation learning
  - Pfam
  - benchmark
